# Testing Conventions (Pest PHP)

## Structure

- Feature tests for HTTP endpoints and full request cycles
- Unit tests for isolated business logic (Services, Actions)
- Test file names mirror the class under test (e.g., `BudgetServiceTest.php`)

## Patterns

- Use `RefreshDatabase` trait for all tests that touch the database
- Use factories for test data — never hardcode database records
- Use `assertInertia()` for verifying Inertia page responses and props
- Group related tests with `describe()` blocks
- Use descriptive test names: `it('calculates monthly budget remaining')`

## Principles

- Each test should test one behavior
- Arrange-Act-Assert structure
- Test both happy path and edge cases
- Mock external services, never hit real APIs in tests
